*  ============================================================================
*  PB-1s PER-SITE SNAPSHOT CELL -- TOP-LEVEL ALTERNATION FORM (s107).
*  RED -- SIG11 both modes (m3 == m4).  Sibling of pb_selfref_alt_cycle.sno; see
*  that file for the full root-cause statement.  THIS form matters because
*  `X = X | Y` in a loop is THE canonical SNOBOL4 idiom for building an
*  alternation set incrementally, so the class is wider than the
*  `X = X (A | B)` spelling alone suggested.  Census (s107, 1305 .sno files)
*  finds the shape in lib/case.sno, csnobol4-suite/atn.sno, gimpel/LIKE.sno,
*  gimpel/OR.sno, lon/sno/{PARSER,Bouvier,TZ,transl8}.sno -- though of those
*  only beauty_suite/case_driver is cleanly fingerprint-confirmed to date
*  (atn.sno is parse-blocked at :360; the gimpel files error in the ORACLE too).
*  Oracle: /home/claude/x64/bin/sbl -b <file>
*  ============================================================================
        mk = 'q'
        n = 0
LP      n = n + 1
        mk = mk | 'y'
        LT(n,2)                         :S(LP)
        'y' mk                          :F(NO)
        OUTPUT = 'MATCHED toplevel'     :(FIN)
NO      OUTPUT = 'NOMATCH toplevel'
FIN
END
